## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-region federation, token lifecycles, and poisoning resistance in a real product.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-region federation with privacy guarantees
- Threshold cryptography (t-of-n) for aggregation
- Token lifecycle, revocation, and immutable audit
- Poisoning resistance via commitments and batch verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal stub for threshold aggregation
function aggregateShares(shares, threshold) {
  // verify shares, then combine if at least threshold reached
  // actual crypto omitted for brevity
  if (shares.length < threshold) throw new Error('Insufficient shares')
  return shares.reduce((a,b)=> a + b, 0) / threshold
}
```

